<title>HONG KONG: Fairyoung 1996 net down 63 percent.</title>
<headline>Fairyoung 1996 net down 63 percent.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   3.2	  vs  9.0</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    nil	  vs  nil</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  50.11 gain vs  55.64 gain</p>
<p>    Net			    10.48	vs  28.57</p>
<p>    Turnover		     73.57	vs  54.69</p>
<p>    Company name		 Fairyoung Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  June 19-25</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   N/A</p>
<p>NOTE - Fairyoung Holdings is a property investment and development and securities trading firm.</p>
<p>Net is after an exceptional gain of HK$43 million on disposal of subscription right of a subsidary, gain of HK$9.29 million from deposits forfeited on sale of properties and loss of HK$2.18 million on provision for diminution of a long-term investment.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is nil vs nil.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
